                "question": "Why is the caisson gate considered the most critical component in a dry dock?",
                "answer": "The caisson gate is the movable structure that seals the dock entrance against open water, and its hinge, sealing mechanism, and structural connection components must reliably hold back the full hydrostatic pressure of the adjacent water body every time the dock is in use. A caisson gate failure represents a genuinely serious operational and safety event given the water volume and structural consequence involved, making its component reliability a facility-critical priority."
