                "question": "Why does an FPSO need both marine structural forgings and process piping forgings?",
                "answer": "An FPSO functions simultaneously as a moored or dynamically positioned marine vessel and as a full onboard oil and gas processing plant, requiring shipbuilding-scale structural forgings for mooring, turret, and hull connection systems alongside process piping, valve, and flange forgings for the onboard processing and storage systems \u2014 two genuinely distinct component categories serving the vessel's dual function."
