        "faqs": [
            {
                "question": "What elevator and lift components does JK Forge manufacture?",
                "answer": "We manufacture traction sheave forgings, deflector sheave forgings, guide shoe brackets, rope anchor plates, car frame brackets, safety gear body blanks, governor rope lever forgings, buffer plunger bodies, machine room mounting brackets and counterweight guide brackets for elevator and lift systems."
            },
            {
                "question": "What materials are used for elevator sheave forgings?",
                "answer": "Traction and deflector sheave blanks are produced in EN8 (also known as SAE 1040 / IS C45) for standard-duty applications and EN19 (SAE 4140) for high-load or high-speed installations. EN8 forgings are typically supplied normalised; EN19 sheave forgings are quench-and-tempered for improved hardness and wear resistance."
            },
            {
                "question": "Can JK Forge supply forged safety gear and governor components with safety documentation?",
                "answer": "Yes. Safety gear body blanks, wedge blanks and governor rope lever forgings are produced with full material test reports (UTS, yield, elongation), hardness test certificates and dimensional inspection reports. Heat traceability from raw material to finished forging is maintained and provided in the documentation package."
            },
            {
                "question": "Does JK Forge supply elevator forgings to Otis, Schindler, Kone or ThyssenKrupp?",
                "answer": "We supply elevator forged components to Tier 1 and Tier 2 suppliers in the Indian manufacturing networks of Otis, Schindler, Kone, ThyssenKrupp and Mitsubishi Elevator. Direct OEM supply is subject to vendor qualification; we support this process with our ISO 9001:2015 quality documentation."
            },
            {
                "question": "What is the advantage of forged sheaves over cast iron sheaves?",
                "answer": "Forged steel sheaves have significantly higher impact resistance, fatigue strength and material consistency than cast iron. In high-rise or high-speed elevator installations where sheave failure would be a safety event, forged EN19 steel sheaves are specified for their superior toughness and predictable mechanical properties under dynamic rope loading."
            },
            {
                "question": "Can JK Forge machine the groove profile on traction sheave forgings?",
                "answer": "Yes, we offer semi-machined and fully machined traction sheave blanks with bore, groove profile and face dimensions machined to drawing. The groove profile \u2014 U-groove or undercut V-groove \u2014 is machined to the wire rope diameter specification provided by the customer."
            },
            {
                "question": "What are your typical lead times for elevator forging components?",
                "answer": "For established tooling on repeat components, lead time is 3\u20135 weeks from order. For new components requiring die development, allow 6\u20138 weeks for tooling plus production. We work with elevator OEM procurement teams on scheduled supply programs to align lead times with installation project schedules."
            },
            {
                "question": "How do I enquire about elevator forging supply from JK Forge?",
                "answer": "Send your component drawings, material and heat treatment specifications, quantity requirements and quality documentation requirements to sales@JK Forge.com or call +91 7600066117. We will assess the requirement and provide a quotation within 24\u201348 hours."
            }
        ]
