                "question": "Why does LNG require special cryogenic-grade materials?",
                "answer": "LNG is stored at approximately \u2212162\u00b0C, and most standard carbon and low-alloy steels undergo a ductile-to-brittle transition at low temperature that can cause sudden, catastrophic fracture. Cryogenic-qualified materials like 9% nickel steel and austenitic stainless steel (304L/316L) retain ductility and impact toughness at these temperatures, making them the required materials for any LNG-wetted component."
