        "description2": "Automotive forgings are manufactured to tolerances and quality requirements that push forging process capability harder than almost any other application. A passenger car steering knuckle must be dimensionally accurate enough to assemble without shimming, strong enough to survive a 30g kerb strike impact, and light enough that the unsprung mass target is met. JK Forge has been developing and manufacturing automotive forgings from its Shapar, Rajkot facility for over 20 years, and the technical discipline built over those years is embedded in our process controls and tooling design practices.",
